data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1182,"item_id":"msg_0812b46a04d5b865016b0312e844f887d18ce8d7210e1d2a98","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"{\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"actor\": \"birch-4\",\n      \"decision\": \"reuse\",\n      \"ability\": \"bark-extraction\",\n      \"reason\": \"The implemented capability already assesses actual material and separates a finite branch outer layer using an inspected stone or flint contact. Its prerequisites, costs and conserved outputs match this request. The observed object represents fallen branch stock, not harvestable standing-tree tissue. Its two branch units are not owned bark, and neither a suitable tool nor successful assessment is established. Individual learning is required.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Reuse the existing bark-extraction contract unchanged, including its public assessment/peeling parameters, source validation, progress and cancellation behavior. Assessment costs one round and 0.2 energy; peeling requires actual eligible material and a personally inspected reusable stone or flint, with two active work-round equivalents and two energy per original intact branch unit, reduced for fractional or already processed material. Use existing gather for exposed branch-stock transfer, charging its actual costs and depletion; do not strip the source object's standing trunk or infer represented living tissue from its kind label. An unspecified intact branch may partition at most 10% of its existing mass into outer bark, with whole tenth-unit bark outputs rounded down and residual mass retained as bark-fines. Preserve core, fines, provenance and remaining work. Enforce shared reach and collision geometry; never teleport inputs. Multi-round work must stop on death, retaining partial processing and returning or grounding actual escrow exactly once under the existing ownership contract. No stock, tool or mastery is granted by review.\",\n      \"experienceReview\": \"Reuse the existing practice:bark-extraction source, not an alias. A successful paid completion emitting practice-confirmed with qualified=true may grant the participating actor 0.4 temporary satisfaction, capped at 0.5 for eight rounds, refreshing with a 12-round cooldown. Qualification requires the existing limited genuine progress milestone with changed physical outputs; application, learning, mastery and routine output alone do not qualify. Its maintained component gains 0.02 on qualifying participation and decays 0.001 per round under the registered rule. A genuinely new experimentally confirmed finding may separately use information-confirmed through probe under grounded-understanding's existing qualification and cooldown rules; a repeated observation does not qualify. Bark possession itself grants no comfort, health or nutritional benefit.\",\n      \"visualReview\": \"Reuse bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped for subscription and replay. Show actual eligibility findings, inspected contact, paid progress, remaining work, separated bark/fines and changed core mass. Source stock changes only on actual transfer; do not depict trunk wounds or tree injury when only represented fallen branches were collected. Show unavailable inputs and failed reach checks without presenting successful extraction.\",\n      \"learning\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"actor\": \"birch-6\",\n      \"decision\": \"reuse\",\n      \"ability\": \"bark-extraction\",\n      \"reason\": \"The existing bark-extraction interface provides the requested assessment and bounded collection mechanism without assuming free bark or stripping an unrepresented trunk. The nearby object exposes nine units of fallen branches; that establishes source stock, not owned or already assessed bark. The two owned stones are possible reusable contacts, but a personally inspected suitable contact and eligible material must still be validated. Root-air-drying mastery does not confer bark-extraction mastery.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Reuse bark-extraction's existing public schema and executable contract without a duplicate implementation. Assessment takes one round and 0.2 energy. Actual eligible branch material and an inspected reusable stone or flint contact are required for peeling; charge two active work-round equivalents and two energy per original intact branch unit, proportionally reduced for actual remaining work. Exposed branch collection uses gather with its existing reach, energy and finite-stock costs. Preserve origin and material accounting: an unspecified intact branch partitions at most 10% of existing mass into outer bark; round bark outputs down to tenth units, retaining the remainder as bark-fines and conserving the peeled core. Do not convert the nine source units into bark in place or injure an unrepresented living trunk. Apply shared geometry and interaction checks. Progress and partial products persist; death cancels active work without cloning or deleting escrow, and releases actual reserved inputs exactly once under the existing contract. Existing stone ownership does not waive inspection, effort or individual learning.\",\n      \"experienceReview\": \"Use the already registered practice:bark-extraction rule for the actual participating actor: qualifying paid completion with a genuine limited progress milestone emits practice-confirmed, granting 0.4 temporary satisfaction capped at 0.5 for eight rounds, refreshable with a 12-round cooldown. Maintain its existing 0.02 gain per qualifying event and 0.001-per-round decay; routine production and mastery alone do not qualify. Do not create a second reward for 'safe collection' or for enabling a drying tray. A new finding actually confirmed through probe may use information-confirmed and the existing grounded-understanding rule, not an additional source. Assessment requests, learning and receiving bark have no automatic wellbeing award; physical benefits depend on later actual use.\",\n      \"visualReview\": \"Bind existing bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped events to observable findings and work. Display actual branch depletion upon collection, reserved stone, processing fraction, conserved core/bark/fines quantities and interruption state in replay. Report that standing-tree injury is inapplicable when processing fallen branch material; do not draw invented trunk damage. No tray or preservation effect is displayed before its separately paid construction and use.\",\n      \"learning\": 2\n    }\n  ]\n}","logprobs":[]}

